  "description": "LEPSIM crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group I 2. Reported CIF formula moiety: C63 H65 Dy6 N6 O37 1-,6(C1 H4 O1),3(H2 O1),H3 O1 1+. From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.605-3.807 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 91.68-113.07°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy6(L2)3(μ3-OH)(OAc)9(H2O)3]·H3O·6MeOH·3H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 9 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 3 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 9 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 3 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
